{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>מאסף</b> (gatherer / rear guard). Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: ואין איש מאסף אותם הביתה (and no man gathered them home) in Judges 19, and וכעמיר מאחרי הקוצר (and like a gleaned sheaf behind the reaper) in Psalms. And there is no מאסף for the tribe of Dan, because the idol of Micah was with them; therefore ואין איש מאסף — the cloud expelled them, and Amalek killed among them, and they fell וכעמיר מאחרי הקוצר, ואין מאסף (and no gatherer)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the idol of Micah' (פסל) refers to Judges 18:30–31; Ba'al HaTurim links the three מאסף occurrences as a sequence: Dan lacks a gatherer because of sin, so the cloud cast them out, Amalek attacked, they fell like gleanings, and none gathered."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:46.746307629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}